; bfsodium SHA_512 HASHCORE : the hash  over a prefix in memory and then the wire
;
; HAND WRITTEN skeleton; The round and the schedule step are each PASTED from
; their own verified files; what is here is the constant table  the padding and
; the conveyors;
;
; TWO THINGS IN THIS FILE ARE NOT TYPED OUT ONE CHARACTER AT A TIME  and it is
; better to say so than to let a reader assume otherwise; The eighty round
; constants and the eight initial words are FIPS 180_4's own numbers  rendered
; as byte deltas by the rule the comment above them states  and they are the
; same table the vectors check; And a run of ONE repeated token  clearing six
; hundred and forty cells or sliding a block down one place  is a repetition
; rather than a decision  which is what Rn is for one level down; Every offset
; every section and every branch below was worked out from the map and written
; down;
;
; INTERFACE entry=259 exit=2028 footprint=0:2051
; IO  in:  plen{2} LE  slen{2} LE  pbuf{256}  then slen bytes from the wire
;     out: digest{64}  big endian  as the standard prints it
;
; The message is plen bytes taken from pbuf  followed by slen bytes read from
; the wire; either count may be nought; Only the first plen bytes of pbuf are
; looked at  and the rest may hold anything;
;
; PBUF IS FOUR HUNDRED AND FORTY EIGHT CELLS BUT THE WIRE FILLS ONLY THE FIRST
; TWO HUNDRED AND FIFTY SIX  which is what the IO line above says and is not a
; mistake; a caller reaching the rest writes it in memory  which is what HMAC
; does and is the only way anything above plen of two hundred and fifty six
; arises; the slide that consumes the prefix covers all four hundred and forty
; eight either way;
;
; TWO SOURCES  because two callers want different ones; sha512 hashes what is
; on the wire and leaves plen at nought; HMAC hashes a block it has built in
; memory  a key exclusive ored with a pad  and then the message; HKDF hashes
; only what it has built  and leaves slen at nought; One padding loop and one
; block loop serve all three;
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000:0x001  plen{2} u16 LE  prefix bytes not yet taken; SPENT
;   @0x002:0x003  slen{2} u16 LE  wire bytes not yet taken; SPENT
;   @0x004:0x1c3  pbuf{448} u8    the prefix; consumed from its head; it was
;                          256 cells until 192 more were inserted above it  and
;                          that insertion is the whole of the change that lifted
;                          HKDF's info allowance from sixty three bytes to 190
;   @0x1c4:0x203  H{8}    u64 LE  the running hash  and then the digest
;   @0x204:0x243  v{8}    u64 LE  a b c d e f g h
;   @0x244:0x2c3  w{16}   u64 LE  the schedule window
;   @0x2c4:0x2d3  Wt and Wc  this round's schedule word and the window's copy
;   @0x2d4:0x2d9  pre rnd f16 nf tt uu   the round counters and their flags
;   @0x2da        iv       u8      the CALLER'S flag: nought for SHA_512's own
;                          initial words  one to say the caller has written H
;                          itself; not spent  so one setting serves all three
;                          of HMAC's entries
;   @0x2e4:0x2e5  the two cells that flag is looked at and branched on through
;   @0x2dc:0x2e3  tmp{8}  hands a word back after it has been copied
;   @0x2e8:0x303  the adder frame; add64 footprint 0:27 at @0x2e8
;   @0x308:0x41c  sha512/round's frame; its footprint is 0:276 pasted there
;   @0x420:0x4e4  sha512/expand's frame; its footprint is 0:196
;   @0x4e8:0x767  K{80}   u64 LE  the constants; the table ROTATES one word per
;                          round  so K{t} is always at its head and after eighty
;                          rounds it is back where it started  which is what
;                          lets a second block use it again
;   @0x768:0x7e7  blk{128} u8     the block being built
;   @0x7ea:0x7f2  the padding's flags  its byte counter and the cells the two
;                          counts are tested through
;   @0x7f4:0x7fb  len{8}  u64 LE  the message length  kept for the last block
;   @0x7fc:0x803  ksave{8}        holds K{t} while the table rotates past it
;
; THE ONE CHOICE THAT MADE THIS PORT TRACTABLE; the flags  the length and ksave
; sit at the SAME offsets above the top of the block as they do in
; sha256/hashcore: onep is three above it  room four  more five  the byte
; counter six  the have flag seven  the else arm eight  the two test cells nine
; and ten  and the second else arm eleven; So every distance in the padding
; machinery measured from the top of the block is the same number in both files
; and only the ones reaching down into plen  slen  pbuf and the frames had to be
; worked out again; Read the two side by side;
;
; The tables are CLEARED before they are written  because writing a byte here
; ADDS to what the cell held; HMAC enters this routine three times over and the
; second entry would otherwise find the first digest still in H and add the
; initial words to it; The constants do survive a call untouched  since the
; table rotates a full eighty places per block and comes back to where it
; started  but they are cleared too: a routine that is safe to enter twice
; should not rest on that being noticed;
;
; The prefix buffer is at the BOTTOM  with the two counts  because a read
; prologue may hold only reads and single steps: a long run of steps before the
; first read is split across lines by the layout pass  and a paste begins at the
; prologue  so those steps would be silently dropped; tools/bffoot refuses a
; routine shaped that way;
;
; FOUR CONVEYORS AND NO INDEX; the schedule window slides so its four taps are
; always in the same cells  the constants rotate so the round always reads the
; head of the table  the block slides so a byte always lands on its top  and
; the prefix is consumed from its head and slides after each byte;
;
; A NOTE ON THE LENGTH; SHA_512 ends a message with a HUNDRED AND TWENTY EIGHT
; bit length where SHA_256 uses sixty four; Only the low eight bytes are ever
; written  because the byte count is kept in four cells and a message of more
; than four gigabytes is not something a brainfuck program is going to be
; handed; the other eight bytes of the field are the nought the block was
; cleared to;

; read the two counts and the prefix buffer
,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,
; ASSERT ptr=259

; ==== the eighty round constants ====
; A table because the rounds are a loop; each line is one constant  eight
; bytes little endian  each byte the shorter of counting up from nought or
; down through the wrap;
; the table is emptied first  so a second entry is safe
R997
